What causes tr→tr? Walk: 27 stops: button, g, button... sequence: 2 header buttons → rail roving (1 button) → g (chart) → 10 sort buttons → ~13 rows (window at 1440×900: visible ≈ (clientH-theadH)/24 ≈ 13) → chips/history? 2+1+1+10+13 = 27 exactly! So the LAST stops are rows — no ledger stops walked (or ledger after 27 cut). The single tr→tr inversion: hmm. Among consecutive rows... 

OH WAIT. I know EXACTLY what it is now! **The self-correcting rowH re-render!** No... During a plain Tab walk, no re-render happens. Hmm.

Consecutive trs with a downward... UNLESS: the spacer rows! The window renders [spacer?, rows..., spacer?]. Rows are DOM-ordered. Tab stops among trs: only data rows (spacers aria-hidden but no tabindex — not tabbable). So tr→tr Tab moves DOWN the table. y increases. Why inversion?!

